+    <h2>1. Overview: Privacy by Design &amp; Data Minimization</h2>
+    <p>
+        At <strong>The DevTools Times</strong>, we follow the principles of <strong>Privacy by Design</strong>, <strong>Data Minimization</strong>, and <strong>User Transparency</strong>. By default, our site operates without non-essential tracking, behavioral profiling, or unconsented third-party scripts.
+    </p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Default Opt-Out for Third-Party Scripts:</strong> Optional third-party analytics and advertising scripts are disabled by default and only run if you explicitly opt in via our Privacy Preferences control.</li>
+        <li><strong>Browser Privacy Signals Honored:</strong> We automatically detect and respect <code>Do Not Track (DNT)</code> and <code>Global Privacy Control (GPC)</code> signals.</li>
+        <li><strong>Minimal Data Collection:</strong> We only collect data strictly necessary to provide the specific feature you request (such as authenticating your account or saving an article to your Reading List).</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>2. Account Registration &amp; Sign-In Data</h2>
+    <p><strong>What we collect and why</strong></p>
